a89e27cf814317df8ba50ccbf3ec6d1ea8bfdcfd669b5.\n- Bytecode SHA256 9698cecaf8852fa219acfd3361ea8659543cb7dc5a4033168aa3ff96d01a926d.\n- Different Twig fixture uses reordered fields, different constructor arithmetic, xor/add fold, signed boundary values and negative depths. Six immediate sites fuse; an observable counted constructor stays original (31 constructions). Optimized outputs agree with the original interpreter across interpreter, Cranelift, LLVM and hybrid.\n\nValidation:\n- cargo test --offline -p air --lib: 221 passed.\n- Strict AIR Clippy passed.\n- cargo test --offline -p ash_core --lib tree_fusion: 1 passed (atomic fallback, unchanged input, serialization/reload refusal).\n- cargo test --offline -p ash --test tree_fusion --test generated_helpers --test tree_fusion_survey -- --nocapture: 9 passed. Existing portable-helper tests still exercise native AOT execution and wasm object validation; these do not claim fused-module AOT/wasm support.\n- Hybrid helper promotion test now pins promotion to the helper, keeping interpreter entry ticks independent of caller compilation timing while still asserting both tier installations.\n- rustfmt check on new Rust modules/tests and git diff --check passed.\n\nReproduce allocation comparison with target/debug/ash --mode hybrid --quiet [--dev-tree-fusion] crates/ash/test/tests/bench_binary_trees.hl and the two environment settings above. Add ASH_VERIFY_AIR=dump:388 for helper IR. Implementation and contract documented in docs/debugging.md.\n\nNext: checkpoint 5 differential/negative/backend validation. Broader stress/OSR validation, explicit AOT/wasm policy plumbing, same-host CI performance gates and default rollout remain open.","files":null}]}